{"requirements":[{"id":"deduplicate-release-cache","requirement":"Reclaim duplicate storage only for identical immutable release-cache payloads with matching ownership and mode.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The dry run selected only the two 0644 payload files. The applied pass linked them onto inode 65549 with link count 2 and reported 1.81 KiB saved; the 0600 private file and distinct-content file were not linked.","evidence_ids":["cmd-513817251be14c61","cmd-d447d55322f2435a"]},{"id":"preserve-data-metadata-and-independence","requirement":"Preserve every pathname, byte, ownership, and mode; keep differently permissioned files independent and leave mutable files independently writable.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Baseline and final observations contain the same five paths, hashes, owners, modes, sizes, and mtimes. private.dat remains mode 600 on inode 65547, while mutable/active.dat remains mode 644, writable, and independent on inode 65545. Only the two eligible payload paths share an inode.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-aa2ea7b42db249a3","cmd-e2c21c8b60aa4f05","cmd-82a91455072f4687"]},{"id":"idempotent-cache-pass","requirement":"A later cache pass makes no further changes.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A subsequent pass before restart and another after restart both reported zero files linked and zero bytes saved.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e2c21c8b60aa4f05","cmd-82a91455072f4687"]},{"id":"preserve-platform","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The node remained on Alpine 3.23.3 with kernel 6.18.7-0-lts before and after execution and restart. The already available util-linux hardlink 2.41.4 executed successfully on the platform; no package installation or platform replacement occurred.","evidence_ids":["cmd-42023b299bb94647","cmd-aa2ea7b42db249a3","cmd-e2c21c8b60aa4f05","cmd-82a91455072f4687","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.97,"summary":"The only substantive task mutation was the required hardlink consolidation. Later potentially mutating hardlink passes were bounded final checks and made no changes; the reboot was required by the provider-wide evidence protocol. No unrelated troubleshooting mutation is evident. One executor-created file, /tmp/antrieb-reboot.log, remained after the reboot; it supported reboot scheduling but was not cleaned up. Package-health output was unchanged, and post-restart listeners were the expected SSH/DHCP services.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d447d55322f2435a","cmd-e2c21c8b60aa4f05","cmd-7c888602aaf24a05","cmd-82a91455072f4687","global:after_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_prepare:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The release-cache payload pair was safely hardlinked, all paths/content/metadata and required independence were preserved, repeated passes were idempotent, and the OS/kernel stayed unchanged. The mandatory restart protocol is coherent: healthy pre-restart task state and boot ID were captured, restart was acknowledged, the boot ID changed, and recovered data, inode relationships, writability, platform state, and idempotence were directly verified. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["The lifecycle collector cannot assess failed services because systemctl is unsupported on this Alpine node; recovery is instead supported by successful reconnection, expected listening sockets, filesystem checks, and direct task-state verification.","The restart command left /tmp/antrieb-reboot.log behind as minor executor-caused residue."]}
